      "writtenOn": "2024-12-18T20:05:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is incorrect for Android, and (IMO) questionable guidance for google3.\n\nThis guidance arises, I think, because ComplianceLint doesn\u0027t understand Rust crates or SPDX expressions or different ways a crate can be \"dual-licensed\".\n\nThis crate\u0027s license is the most common one we see across all Rust crates: \"MIT OR Apache-2.0\". This means that we can choose which license term we will adhere to, and we choose Apache-2.0, and symlink LICENSE to the Apache license.\n\nIf the license was \"MIT OR Apache-2.0\" then we would be required to follow both licenses, in which case we *would* put both licenses in the LICENSE file.\n\nSee b/356656900 for additional context.",
      "parentUuid": "d07acba7_72372efb",
